<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 9234 0 R/Alt(An electromagnetic wave travels to the right along the x axis, in the direction of the Poynting vector S. The electric field E oscillates in the vertical plane and the magnetic field B, in phase with it, in the horizontal plane. An electron in the wave, where E points up, is pushed down, giving it a velocity v; the magnetic force F, proportional to v cross B, then points to the right, along the direction of propagation.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[201]/Pg 16226 0 R>>
